cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived district estimates, please cite the paper."
title: "India Household Energy: comparing, calibrating and using district LPG estimates"
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline for evaluating, calibrating and augmenting the single
  cooking-fuel question in India's National Family Health Survey against two
  dedicated household energy surveys (ACCESS, IRES) and the NSS 78th-round
  Multiple Indicator Survey, and for propagating the resulting exposure
  uncertainty into district-level child-mortality analyses.
type: software
license: ISC
repository-code: "https://github.com/pdez90/India_householdenergy"
authors:
  - family-names: deSouza
    given-names: Priyanka
keywords:
  - exposure assessment
  - measurement error
  - clean cooking
  - household air pollution
  - small-area estimation
  - India
